            <ArticleTitle>Vibrational spectroscopic study of fluticasone propionate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>244-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.saa.2008.08.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fluticasone propionate is a synthetic glucocorticoid with potent anti-inflammatory activity that has been used effectively in the treatment of chronic asthma. The present work reports a vibrational spectroscopic study of fluticasone propionate and gives proposed molecular assignments on the basis of ab initio calculations using BLYP density functional theory with a 6-31G* basis set and vibrational frequencies predicted within the quasi-harmonic approximation. Several spectral features and band intensities are explained. This study generated a library of information that can be employed to aid the process monitoring of fluticasone propionate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
